  "scope": "Mandatory scoped journal writer token in internal HID transfer; target/hold/current-file validation before query, durable marker before PWM, final outcome before reply. No user updater/global coordinator/unlock or downgrade anchor.",
  "implementation": {
    "command": "FirmwareUpdate requires boxed owned ArmedOperation, no Clone/Deserialize/reopen API. Actor tree binds HID actor to its PersistenceStore journal scope; ordinary unscoped low-level actor refuses update before any query/write. Box bounds mailbox enum size.",
    "binding": "Exact store root, supported VID/PID, normalized serial/path/settings-key, explicit hold, Armed state and unchanged raw journal bytes checked before readonly cmd134. Empty serial normalized to same singleton convention as settings_key. Original FD metadata, not post-flash freshness proof.",
    "effects": "After supported current identity preflight and before PWM, effects_possible() must complete file/directory fsync. Marker covers all later holds/chunks/activation even without progress checkpoint.",
    "finish": "Normal/failure outcomes persisted before result/progress published. Commit failure forces Unknown and preserves write/attempted counters, even after valid activation reply. Panic may leave EffectsPossible; all stages remain quarantined. EffectsPossible cannot be downgraded to NotStarted by metadata finish.",
    "registry": "Journal digest now references shared Rust pinned image digest instead of duplicated constant.",
    "scope_limits": "Internal helpers still need coordinator enforcing checked quiescence, global admission and snapshot freshness. Legacy/debug raw transport is outside firmware update command contract; product update entry absent."
  },
